  "/faq/boq-generator": [
    {
      "q": "Where do the BOQ lines come from?",
      "a": "From the calculators. Each line records what was measured, in the unit that trade is measured in, at the quantity the calculation produced. The descriptions come from the measurement rather than from a template, which is what makes a line defensible when a client queries it. Nothing appears in the bill that was not measured somewhere in the system."
    },
    {
      "q": "Are contingency and tax added automatically?",
      "a": "Contingency is a line you add, and tax is reported as undetermined unless a rule applies to your market. Neither is applied silently, because a bill is a document a client prices against and a client is entitled to see what is in it. A contingency folded into rates is invisible, and an assumed tax rate is wrong in most jurisdictions it is applied to."
    },
    {
      "q": "Can I defend a line to a client?",
      "a": "Yes, and that is the point of generating rather than typing. The line carries the quantity, the unit and the description that produced it, so a query about the blockwork can be answered with a wall length, a height, an opening schedule and a block size. A bill that cannot be defended line by line is a negotiation rather than an estimate."
    },
    {
      "q": "Does it replace a quantity surveyor?",
      "a": "No. A quantity surveyor measures, prices risk, structures contracts and takes responsibility for the figures. The generator presents measured work as a bill, which removes the transcription step and the errors that come with it. It does not replace the judgement about what to measure, how to price the risk or how to structure the contract."
    },
    {
      "q": "What if an estimate changes after the quote?",
      "a": "The lines regenerate. A changed measurement produces a changed line, and the rates you set stay where they are, so the bill reflects the new quantity at the price you had agreed with yourself. Where a change was agreed with the client, that is a variation rather than a regeneration, and it needs its own record so the original bill remains visible."
    }
  ],
